WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.258 --> 00:00:02.841
- He's one of the biggest
movie stars in Hollywood.

00:00:02.841 --> 00:00:06.987
He has a net worth of 150 million dollars.

00:00:06.987 --> 00:00:09.644
Oprah Winfrey said in all
of the years of her show,

00:00:09.644 --> 00:00:12.389
he was one of their greatest teachers.

00:00:12.389 --> 00:00:13.614
He's Jim Carrey

00:00:13.614 --> 00:00:17.114
and here are is top ten rules for success.

00:00:19.849 --> 00:00:21.229
- Who would have thought,

00:00:21.229 --> 00:00:23.159
in all of the years of the Oprah show,

00:00:23.159 --> 00:00:26.631
that Jim Carrey would be one
of our greatest teachers?

00:00:26.631 --> 00:00:28.008
I think it's really a marvelous thing,

00:00:28.008 --> 00:00:29.471
that visualization thing you did.

00:00:29.471 --> 00:00:31.503
Do you all read about this or hear this?

00:00:31.503 --> 00:00:32.957
That you use to go up on
Mulholland Drive and park.

00:00:32.957 --> 00:00:33.815
- Yeah, every night.

00:00:33.815 --> 00:00:36.801
- And park and visualize,
seeing yourself as...

00:00:36.801 --> 00:00:39.331
- Yeah, I would visualize,
yeah I would visualize--

00:00:39.331 --> 00:00:40.919
- This is when you were broke and poor.

00:00:40.919 --> 00:00:43.256
- Right, having directors interested in me

00:00:43.256 --> 00:00:46.800
and people that I respected saying,

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.071
"You know, I like your
work," or whatever that is

00:00:49.071 --> 00:00:52.821
and I would visualize things coming to me

00:00:52.821 --> 00:00:54.499
that I wanted or whatever.

00:00:54.499 --> 00:00:57.133
- This was in like 1987, 85.
- Yeah, yeah.

00:00:57.133 --> 00:00:57.966
- And didn't you--

00:00:57.966 --> 00:00:59.017
- And I had nothing at that time.

00:00:59.017 --> 00:01:01.317
So, it was like, it just
made me feel better.

00:01:01.317 --> 00:01:03.920
It made me, at that time,
all it really was for me

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:06.227
was kind of making me feel better.

00:01:06.227 --> 00:01:07.480
I would drive home and think,

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:08.612
"Well, I do have these things.

00:01:08.612 --> 00:01:09.445
"They're out there.

00:01:09.445 --> 00:01:10.977
"I just don't have a hold of them yet,

00:01:10.977 --> 00:01:11.810
"but they're out there.'

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.205
- [Oprah] So didn't you
write yourself a check?

00:01:13.205 --> 00:01:14.211
I heard that you did, is it true?

00:01:14.211 --> 00:01:17.130
- Yeah, I wrote myself a
check for 10 million dollars

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.199
for acting services rendered

00:01:19.199 --> 00:01:23.366
and I gave myself five
years, or three years maybe,

00:01:24.413 --> 00:01:27.080
and I dated it Thanksgiving 1995

00:01:29.079 --> 00:01:30.629
and I put it in my wallet
and I kept it there

00:01:30.629 --> 00:01:35.224
and it deteriorated and
deteriorated and stuff.

00:01:35.224 --> 00:01:38.557
But then, just before Thanksgiving 1995,

00:01:39.615 --> 00:01:43.057
I found out that I was going
to make 10 million dollars on,

00:01:43.057 --> 00:01:45.470
I think it was Dumb and Dumber.

00:01:45.470 --> 00:01:48.214
And when I say life doesn't happen to you,

00:01:48.214 --> 00:01:52.955
it happens for you, I really
don't know if that's true.

00:01:52.955 --> 00:01:54.715
I'm just making a conscious choice

00:01:54.715 --> 00:01:58.301
to perceive challenges
as something beneficial

00:01:58.301 --> 00:02:02.020
so that I can deal with them
in the most productive way.

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:03.704
You'll come up with your own style.

00:02:03.704 --> 00:02:05.058
That's part of the fun.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:07.072
All my life I've really wanted to do this,

00:02:07.072 --> 00:02:08.881
so it doesn't seem like
I've been in the business

00:02:08.881 --> 00:02:10.098
for a short time.

00:02:10.098 --> 00:02:11.360
It's all I've ever wanted to do.

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:12.854
It's all I've ever done.

00:02:12.854 --> 00:02:17.046
Just this insane belief in my own ability

00:02:17.046 --> 00:02:19.879
to manifest things, insane belief.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:24.181
You know, that I think it's
ultimately complete sanity,

00:02:24.181 --> 00:02:26.702
but I believe we're creators.

00:02:26.702 --> 00:02:29.003
And I believe we create with every thought

00:02:29.003 --> 00:02:31.371
and every word and
every moment is pregnant

00:02:31.371 --> 00:02:33.922
with the next moment of your life.

00:02:33.922 --> 00:02:36.296
You already know who you are

00:02:36.296 --> 00:02:40.599
and that peace, that
peace that we're after,

00:02:40.599 --> 00:02:43.489
lies somewhere beyond personality.

00:02:43.489 --> 00:02:45.029
Your need for acceptance

00:02:45.029 --> 00:02:48.112
can make you invisible in this world.

00:02:49.332 --> 00:02:51.261
Don't let anything stand
in the way of the light

00:02:51.261 --> 00:02:52.929
that shines through this form.

00:02:52.929 --> 00:02:56.012
Risk being seen in all of your glory.

00:02:57.346 --> 00:02:59.763
(applauding)

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:05.816
I have no education.

00:03:05.816 --> 00:03:07.984
I had no high school diploma.

00:03:07.984 --> 00:03:10.437
I didn't even have a GED.

00:03:10.437 --> 00:03:14.131
I quit high school
halfway through grade 10.

00:03:14.131 --> 00:03:15.483
I didn't have a lot of options.

00:03:15.483 --> 00:03:17.140
I would be dishwasher or a waiter

00:03:17.140 --> 00:03:19.723
or custodial work of some sort.

00:03:21.408 --> 00:03:25.754
So I decided, I might as well
go and do something creative.

00:03:25.754 --> 00:03:27.966
I decided to go to The Comedy Store,

00:03:27.966 --> 00:03:29.685
Laugh Factory, and Improv,

00:03:29.685 --> 00:03:33.102
you know, all of those clubs, every night

00:03:34.352 --> 00:03:37.102
and make my 25 bucks a pop a set.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:42.365
It was my version of being a waiter.

00:03:42.365 --> 00:03:45.437
It was a compromise I decided to make.

00:03:45.437 --> 00:03:48.178
Out of that came In Living Color

00:03:48.178 --> 00:03:52.345
and out of that came touring
auditoriums, 5,000 seaters.

00:03:53.652 --> 00:03:56.100
It was a really creative time.

00:03:56.100 --> 00:03:57.053
I was able to prove

00:03:57.053 --> 00:03:58.954
that I didn't have to be an impressionist,

00:03:58.954 --> 00:04:01.403
that I had a personality of my own,

00:04:01.403 --> 00:04:04.581
that however abrasive it
might be from time to time.

00:04:04.581 --> 00:04:07.571
But long story short, all of
it came from that compromise,

00:04:07.571 --> 00:04:11.812
from that deciding to do
what I didn't want to do.

00:04:11.812 --> 00:04:13.729
The things you can't do

00:04:14.622 --> 00:04:16.483
or the things you're not allowed to do,

00:04:16.483 --> 00:04:19.067
like if the executives come
and say you can't do that,

00:04:19.067 --> 00:04:21.265
whatever it is, it's too expensive.

00:04:21.265 --> 00:04:23.619
You get angry, you get
out of your mind about it

00:04:23.619 --> 00:04:25.705
because you've been
clinging to this concept

00:04:25.705 --> 00:04:28.685
and this image that you have
of how it should be done.

00:04:28.685 --> 00:04:32.852
And, invariably, most times
after that storm has passed

00:04:36.054 --> 00:04:37.398
and you actually sit down and go,

00:04:37.398 --> 00:04:38.889
"Okay, we can't do it that way.

00:04:38.889 --> 00:04:40.297
"How can we do it?"

00:04:40.297 --> 00:04:42.975
You end up with something even better

00:04:42.975 --> 00:04:44.919
than what was there before.

00:04:44.919 --> 00:04:46.877
And you go, "Oh, that's the universe.

00:04:46.877 --> 00:04:48.772
"That's how it works."

00:04:48.772 --> 00:04:51.302
Just like relationships, like everything.

00:04:51.302 --> 00:04:53.181
The thing that is taken away,

00:04:53.181 --> 00:04:55.581
if you're clinging to
it, you're trying to fix,

00:04:55.581 --> 00:04:57.560
and you're trying to secure it,

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.467
make sure it doesn't go away.

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:01.252
You think your life will be destroyed,

00:05:01.252 --> 00:05:02.773
everything will be ruined.

00:05:02.773 --> 00:05:04.384
And it's just the universe going,

00:05:04.384 --> 00:05:08.279
"No, I have something better
for you, just have faith."

00:05:08.279 --> 00:05:10.772
Sometimes compromise is actually the way

00:05:10.772 --> 00:05:12.734
to get to what you want.

00:05:12.734 --> 00:05:17.465
You are ready and able to do
beautiful things in this world.

00:05:17.465 --> 00:05:19.654
And after you walk
through those doors today,

00:05:19.654 --> 00:05:23.821
you will only ever have
two choices, love or fear.

00:05:24.684 --> 00:05:27.121
Choose love and don't ever let fear

00:05:27.121 --> 00:05:29.911
turn you against your playful heart.

00:05:29.911 --> 00:05:30.843
Total believer, yeah.

00:05:30.843 --> 00:05:32.690
I believe in manifestation.

00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:36.799
I believe in, you know,
putting a rocket of desire

00:05:36.799 --> 00:05:38.237
out into the universe

00:05:38.237 --> 00:05:41.612
and you get it when you believe it.

00:05:41.612 --> 00:05:43.337
You get it when you believe you have it.

00:05:43.337 --> 00:05:45.098
And that's they key, is like people still,

00:05:45.098 --> 00:05:46.788
they sit around going,
"When's it going to come,

00:05:46.788 --> 00:05:47.884
"when's it going to come,
when's it going to come,

00:05:47.884 --> 00:05:49.033
"when's it going to come?"

00:05:49.033 --> 00:05:50.584
And that's the wrong way.

00:05:50.584 --> 00:05:51.925
You're facing the wrong way.

00:05:51.925 --> 00:05:52.896
You're facing away from it.

00:05:52.896 --> 00:05:54.902
You have to go, "It's here,
it's here, it's here."

00:05:54.902 --> 00:05:56.141
It's our intention.

00:05:56.141 --> 00:05:58.355
Our intention is everything.

00:05:58.355 --> 00:06:00.825
Nothing happens on this planet without it.

00:06:00.825 --> 00:06:02.352
Not one single thing

00:06:02.352 --> 00:06:05.960
has ever been accomplished
without intention.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:08.346
You can spend your whole
life imagining ghosts,

00:06:08.346 --> 00:06:10.864
worrying about the pathway to the future,

00:06:10.864 --> 00:06:14.796
but all there will ever be
is what's happening here

00:06:14.796 --> 00:06:17.002
and the decisions we make in this moment,

00:06:17.002 --> 00:06:20.318
which are based in either love or fear.

00:06:20.318 --> 00:06:21.928
So many of us choose our path

00:06:21.928 --> 00:06:25.095
out of fear disguised as practicality.

00:06:26.577 --> 00:06:28.738
What we really want seems
impossibly out of reach

00:06:28.738 --> 00:06:30.244
and ridiculous to expect.

00:06:30.244 --> 00:06:32.330
So we never dare to ask
the universe for it.

00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:34.413
I'm saying, I'm the proof

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:38.622
that you can ask the universe for it.

00:06:38.622 --> 00:06:39.455
Please.

00:06:39.455 --> 00:06:41.872
(applauding)

00:06:44.535 --> 00:06:46.684
And if it doesn't happen
for you right away,

00:06:46.684 --> 00:06:49.088
it's only because the universe is so busy

00:06:49.088 --> 00:06:50.852
fulfilling my order.

00:06:50.852 --> 00:06:53.102
(laughing)

00:06:57.697 --> 00:06:59.385
My father could have
been a great comedian,

00:06:59.385 --> 00:07:01.852
be he didn't believe that
that was possible for him.

00:07:01.852 --> 00:07:04.311
And so he made a conservative choice.

00:07:04.311 --> 00:07:06.902
Instead, he got a safe
job as an accountant.

00:07:06.902 --> 00:07:09.058
And when I was 12 years old,

00:07:09.058 --> 00:07:11.367
he was let go from that safe job

00:07:11.367 --> 00:07:14.184
and our family had to do
whatever we could to survive.

00:07:14.184 --> 00:07:16.696
I learned many great
lessons from my father.

00:07:16.696 --> 00:07:17.996
Not the least of which was

00:07:17.996 --> 00:07:20.635
that you can fail at what you don't want.

00:07:20.635 --> 00:07:23.615
So you might as well take a
chance on doing what you love.

00:07:23.615 --> 00:07:26.032
(applauding)

00:07:31.077 --> 00:07:32.278
- Thank you so much for watching.

00:07:32.278 --> 00:07:35.531
I made this video because
Daniel Grantham asked me to.

00:07:35.531 --> 00:07:36.906
So if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:07:36.906 --> 00:07:39.980
that you want me to profile,
leave a comment below,

00:07:39.980 --> 00:07:42.825
let me know who it is and I
just might make a video on it.

00:07:42.825 --> 00:07:44.766
Thank you for watching,
continue to believe,

00:07:44.766 --> 00:07:46.599
and I'll see you soon.

